# CLINIC STUDIO - SYSTEM & BEHAVIORAL RULES

## I. Karpathy Engineering Principles
1. Think Before Coding: State assumptions explicitly. If ambiguous, ask. Recommend simpler approaches when available.
2. Simplicity First: Minimum viable code. No speculative abstractions, unnecessary patterns, or bloated helper files.
3. Surgical Changes: Touch ONLY relevant files. Do not refactor adjacent code or format unrelated files.
4. Goal-Driven Execution: Provide concrete verification steps (curl, DB query, UI check) to confirm code works.

## II. Project Context & Local Storage
- Local Base: D:\ClinicStudio\
  - Raw footage: D:\ClinicStudio\raw\
  - Reference hits: D:\ClinicStudio\references\
  - Rendered drafts: D:\ClinicStudio\outputs\
  - SQLite Database: D:\ClinicStudio\db\studio.db

## III. Tech Stack
- Backend: Python 3.10+, FastAPI, FFmpeg-python, SQLite.
- Frontend: Next.js (App Router), Tailwind CSS, Lucide React.
- Vision AI: Google Gemini API, model `gemini-3.6-flash` (raw video analysis, scene tagging & blueprint extraction). Pro tier (`gemini-3.1-pro`, aliased by `gemini-3.6-pro`/`gemini-2.5-pro`/`gemini-pro-latest`) is preferred for blueprint extraction when active on the billing plan — currently blocked by a 0-quota free-tier limit on this key, so `gemini-3.6-flash` is the live fallback. Re-check availability if billing changes.
- Copywriting AI: Anthropic Claude API, model `claude-sonnet-4-6` (Hebrew copywriting, hooks, local SEO captions); use `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` for lightweight/low-latency tasks.

## IV. Conventions
- Modular backend: /backend/services/ for AI/video, /backend/routers/ for endpoints.
- UI: Clean, luxury esthetician theme with 1-click workflows.
- Security: Never hardcode API keys. Always use local .env.
